 ## Operating characteristics
 **Time and Memory Complexity:**
-*   Memory: Approximately 3x less than a full stack. With a short stack of 5 entries, storage is less than 44 bytes (root 64 bits, current node 32 bits, restart trail 3x32 bits, current depth 5 bits, stack entries 5x32 bits) [S1, unofficial]. A full stack with max depth 32 requires 136 bytes [S1, unofficial].
-*   Time: Overhead in traversal steps is 1-10% for closest-hit queries and 0-5% for any-hit queries with a short stack of 5 entries [S1, unofficial]. Quad intersections are reduced by 2-14% [S1, unofficial].
